cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OmicChain, please cite it as below."
title: "OmicChain: certified, verifiable RNA-seq differential expression analyses"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guichet
    given-names: Pierre-Olivier
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0115-2199"
    affiliation: "UR24144 ProDiCeT, Université de Poitiers / CHU de Poitiers, France"
version: 1.0.0-rc1
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: LGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/UR24144-ProDiCeT/OmicChain"
url: "https://ur24144-prodicet.github.io/OmicChain/"
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - differential expression
  - reproducibility
  - research integrity
  - provenance
  - blockchain
  - RO-Crate
abstract: >-
  OmicChain runs an RNA-seq differential expression analysis (Rsubread, DESeq2) from a public study,
  FASTQ files or a count matrix, hashes every component (code, parameters, input data, data origin, R
  environment, results) into one composite SHA-256 fingerprint, publishes it on the Base blockchain and
  produces a certificate and an RO-Crate. Anyone can check the fingerprint and re-run the analysis, from
  the expression table or from the raw data.
